  "worked_solution": "Isolating the cubic-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{3}+5 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x-6)^{3} & \\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the third root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-6)^{3}} & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x-6 & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
